# HOWTO — REQ-011

## Prerequisites
- Node 20+
- npm
- repository/workspace con dipendenze frontend installabili
- React, Next.js 14, TypeScript 5, TanStack Query, Vitest, Testing Library
- backend locale FastAPI oppure endpoint AWS EU per il profilo target

## Runtime Profiles
Profili supportati:
- `local`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_RUNTIME_PROFILE=local`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_INBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=15000`
- `aws`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_RUNTIME_PROFILE=aws`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://workflow-api.eu-region.example.internal`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_INBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=0`

La UI resta identica nei due profili; cambia solo la configurazione dell’adapter HTTP.

## Environment Setup
Preparazione consigliata:
1. portarsi alla root del repository
2. impostare timezone UTC se si vuole output test uniforme
3. creare la cartella artefatti:
   `mkdir -p runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts`

Endpoint richiesti dal modulo:
- `GET /workflow/tasks?status=open`
- `POST /workflow/tasks/{taskId}/read`
- `POST /documents/{documentId}/retry`

## Install
Comando:
`npm ci`

Nota:
- usare mirror npm interno o registry approvato, coerente con i vincoli enterprise
- non servono segreti frontend dedicati per questo REQ

## Local Run Commands
Test completi local profile:
`NEXT_PUBLIC_RUNTIME_PROFILE=local NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 NEXT_PUBLIC_INBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=15000 npx vitest run runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/api.test.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/runtime.test.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/stateBadge.test.tsx runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/taskInbox.test.tsx runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/workflowInbox.browser-smoke.test.tsx --reporter=verbose | tee runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts/vitest.log`

Typecheck:
`npx tsc --jsx react-jsx --module esnext --target es2022 --moduleResolution bundler --lib es2022,dom --noEmit runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/shared/query/runtime.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/shared/ui/stateBadge.tsx runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/workflow/inbox/types.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/workflow/inbox/api.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/workflow/inbox/useTaskInbox.ts runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/workflow/inbox/TaskInbox.tsx runs/kit/REQ-011/src/node/frontend/app/workflow/inbox/page.tsx 2>&1 | tee runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts/typecheck.log`

Cosa si valida localmente:
- lista task aperti
- badge stati workflow
- gating retry
- open action da riga task con href documento stabile
- read state ottimistico, rollback su errore e refresh senza full page reload
- error state ed empty state
- contratto HTTP reale dell’adapter
- risoluzione profilo runtime local/aws

## Target Runtime Commands
Smoke con profilo target configurato:
`NEXT_PUBLIC_RUNTIME_PROFILE=aws NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://workflow-api.eu-region.example.internal NEXT_PUBLIC_INBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=0 npx vitest run runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/runtime.test.ts --reporter=verbose | tee runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts/vitest-aws-profile.log`

Wiring target runtime:
- promuovere i file in `src/` e `tests/` canonici
- collegare `page.tsx` al router/app tree Next.js del repo
- impostare `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` verso il backend AWS EU
- mantenere stesso contratto backend dei path sopra elencati

Dipendenze reali vs locali:
- locale: backend FastAPI locale oppure mock API in test
- target: backend AWS EU reale
- nessun cambio di DTO o componente tra i due profili

## Reports and Artifacts
Report generati dai comandi:
- `runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts/vitest.log`
- `runs/kit/REQ-011/test/node/workflow-inbox/.artifacts/typecheck.log`
